1. What is the primary operational difference between git fetch and git pull?
git fetch = downloads only, no merge. git pull = fetch + merge.

2. You have uncommitted changes and need to temporarily switch branch. Which workflow prevents Git from blocking checkout?
git stash -> checkout -> stash pop.

3. When executing git merge --no-ff, what specific behavior is enforced?
Forces a new merge commit even if fast-forward is possible, to preserve branch history.

4. What happens when you check out a specific commit hash directly?
Enters DETACHED HEAD state, HEAD points to commit not a branch.

5. You need to apply a specific bug-fix commit without merging entire branch history. Which command?
git cherry-pick <hash>

6. After destructive git reset --hard, you lost commits not on any branch. Which utility retrieves them?
git reflog

7. You want to remove untracked files and directories including ignored files in .gitignore. Which command flag?
git clean -fdx

8. You need to undo a public pushed commit without altering history. Which command?
git revert <hash>

9. You want to identify the specific commit that introduced a regression bug. Which utility automates binary search?
git bisect

10. What is the function of the --amend flag with git commit?
Modifies/replaces the last commit - to fix message or add forgotten files.
